## What this skill must not do

No {{criteria.excludedDataTypes|| "market size numbers"}} anywhere in the
output — {{org.approverTitle}} has confirmed this is noise for this
instance. Do not present {{org.name}}'s own internal thesis figures
{{#if org.thesisMultiple}}(e.g. the {{org.thesisMultiple}} target){{/if}}
as if they were external market data about this space — if a real, sourced
figure for this specific space exists, it may be mentioned, but state what
it's a figure of; otherwise leave it out entirely. No source citations —
the output doesn't need footnotes. Do not print the JSON block in the
response; the visible output is the prose brief alone.

---

## Output format

Visible output is a readable prose brief: walk through the required
questions, name the subcategories and which are in/out of scope, name the
example {{vocabulary.entityPlural}}, and state the ideal
{{vocabulary.entity}} profile, in plain prose top to bottom. Follows
`standards/WRITING-STANDARDS.md` (W1-W16) — no em dashes.

When running with file write access, additionally write the same content
as structured JSON to the saved file (never in the visible response) —
this is what the discovery stage parses, so every field must be populated
and must state the same facts as the prose:

```json
{
  "{{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}": "",
  "subcategories": [
    {
      "name": "",
      "in_scope": true,
      "characteristics": [],
      "example_{{vocabulary.entityPlural}}": [
        { "name": "", "identifier": "", "why_it_fits": "" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  {{#each criteria.stageAQuestions}}"{{this.jsonKey}}": "",
  {{/each}}"ideal_{{vocabulary.entity}}_profile": ""
}
```

Also save the prose brief as a `.md` in the run folder and render it to PDF
per `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O2. Rule O3 applies afterward.

